Adesh, as a Lead, I’m going to give you the "cleanest" architectural answer. In a professional system, you don't create a different event for every person you want to notify. Instead, you follow the "Single Source of Truth" event pattern.
For the task creation process, you should create one single event, but design it so that multiple services can use it.
🏛️ 1. The "One Event, Many Listeners" Strategy
Instead of creating a NotificationEvent and a LoggingEvent, you create one TASK_CREATED event.
Think of it like a newspaper. The journalist (your Task Service) writes one story. The readers (Notification Service, Search Indexer, Analytics Service) all read the same story but do different things with it.
🏛️ 2. What exactly goes in the Event?
To make this event "detailed" enough for everyone, your TaskCreatedEvent DTO should look like this:
